 "issues": [
  "u126-u143: 'Scope, Sequence and Content of the Grades and Courses' overview paragraphs labeled examples per grade; HS paragraphs (u138-u143) cover two or more courses each so labeled course null, grades 9-12 (US History I and II together, World History I and II together, electives).",
  "u387: Grade 2 title and introductory narrative are merged in one unit (also contains a stray sentence about CCR anchor standards); labeled examples. Same for u631 (Grade 5 title + narrative).",
  "u196-u202, u247-u252, u319-u321, u388-u390, u445-u446, u549, u632-u633, u761-u762, u865-u868, u950-u958, u1133-u1134: sidebar list of the seven Practice standards, split across units; the end of practice 7 is merged with the asterisk footnote in u202, u252, u321, u390, u868, u958 (labeled standards PK-12). Standalone asterisk footnotes (u455, u552, u637, u765, u1136) labeled backup.",
  "u177: footnote 15 (definition of civic knowledge) labeled backup though it attaches to Practice standard 1.",
  "u185: end of Practice standard 7 merged with the heading 'History and Social Science and the Standards for Literacy'; labeled standards PK-12.",
  "u198-u201, u249-u251, u320, u389, u447-u454, u550-u551, u634-u636, u763-u764, u866, u952-u957, u1135: topic overview lists combined with literacy note and 'Looking Back, Looking Ahead' text; labeled examples (topic headings are repeated in the Content Standards pages).",
  "u212, u217, u289, u290, u464, u465, u473, u508, u673, u688, u697, u776, u935, u1178: clarification statement and the next standard share a unit; labeled standards when a standard is included, examples when clarification only (u673 clarification plus primary sources = examples).",
  "u206, u209, u219, u257, u277, u287, u325, u339, u343, u355, u394-u395, u482, u489, u493, u570, u654, u670, u674, u683, u704-u705: topic headings merged with Supporting Question or a standard; labeled standards.",
  "u653, u682, u965, u975, u1183, u1187, u511, u904: units mix the end of a standard with Key/Suggested Primary Sources lists and/or the next Topic heading; labeled standards (units not split).",
  "u818-u839: one-column table 'Suggested Primary and Secondary Sources for Topic 3' (Grade 6); each row is a unit; labeled examples grade 6.",
  "u921-u931: Grade 7 Greek accomplishments list (7a-7e) extracted as scattered x-positioned fragments in non-reading order; labeled standards grade 7 as a block.",
  "u793-u795: Code of Hammurabi sub-item e. extracted out of order (u795 text belongs before u794); labeled standards grade 6.",
  "u942-u945: 'A Renewed Mission' page repeated between Grade 7 and Grade 8 (page 103); labeled backup, grades all.",
  "u997-u998: Grade 8 Topic 5 heading split ('of the Constitution.' continues standard 11 / heading in u998); both standards 8.",
  "u1009-u1040: Supreme Court cases and holdings under Grade 8 Topic 5 standard 6 are 'for example' lists; labeled examples (they could arguably be part of the standard, content lists). The a./b./c. headings (u1007-u1008, u1018-u1019, u1031-u1032) labeled standards.",
  "u747-u757: middle-grades introduction split into 6-8 title, 6-7 purposes and Grade 8 civics purposes; labeled backup.",
  "u1131-u1136: US History I intro page; the Practice sidebar (u1133-u1134) is course null grades PK-12, while the remaining unit labels carry course 'United States History I'.",
  "u1193-u1194 do not appear in the view (furniture or absent); range ends effectively at u1192 mid Topic 7 standard 5 (items a-j); u1195 (item k) belongs to part 2."
